The premise here doesn't hold for this endpoint — `PUT /api/config` does a partial merge, not a default-reset. In `transports/bifrost-http/handlers/config.go` (the auth-mode update block):

```go
// Only update each field when explicitly provided so partial /api/config
// payloads do not clear stored values ...
if payload.ClientConfig.MCPServerAuthMode != "" {
    updatedConfig.MCPServerAuthMode = payload.ClientConfig.MCPServerAuthMode
}
```

An omitted `mcp_server_auth_mode` preserves the stored boot mode (`currentConfig.MCPServerAuthMode`); it does not revert to the `headers` schema default. This folder runs only in `both`/`oauth` boots, so the mode stays `both`/`oauth` across this PUT.

The flag is also already isolated: the preceding step "Session JWT connects while auth is not enforced" asserts the same token in the same mode is accepted (not 401) before the flip, and this step asserts 401 after. So the 401 is attributable solely to `enforce_auth_on_inference`, not to a mode reset. The test asserts 401 for the right reason.
